+## Changed in stage 2 (gate wired and tested)
 
-- Package names, binaries, identifiers and UI strings are still upstream's.
+- Model calls: Quickstart offers `openvault` first, labeled as the Netie default.
+  It writes one entry, `[providers.models.custom.openvault]`, with
+  `uri = "${NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL}/v1"` (default `http://127.0.0.1:5000/v1`) and no
+  `api_key` field. A key on that entry is refused: OpenVault holds every key.
+  Vendor families stay selectable but are not the default.
+- Subscription logins off (DR-0002 rule 6): the `copilot`, `gemini_cli`,
+  `grok_cli` and `kilocli` families are not offered and the provider factory
+  refuses them; the Codex login and Claude setup-token auth modes are refused;
+  the `claude_code`, `claude_code_runner`, `codex_cli`, `gemini_cli` and
+  `opencode_cli` tools never run.
+- Tools: every tool call, at the one execution point
+  (`crates/zeroclaw-runtime/src/agent/tool_execution.rs`), asks OpenVault
+  `POST /api/crew/gate` with ids only (`kind=runtime`, tool id, `intent=invoke`,
+  turn id, call id). No arguments leave. No answer, a transport error or anything
+  but `allowed: true` is a refusal, returned as the tool result
+  (`Refused by Netie gate: ...`), so the model and the operator see it. Payloads
+  carrying `skill_body`, `prompt`, `instructions` or `transcript` are refused;
+  the HITL write set needs `operator_confirm: true`.
+- Session state persists ids only: the default `session_backend` is `ids-only`.
+  Each stored message keeps its role and a short sha256, never its text.
+  `sqlite` and `jsonl` still exist and are labeled ungoverned in the schema docs.
+- Channels: the CLI stays local. Every other configured channel instance asks
+  OpenVault leave-machine (`kind=service`, `id=channel.<type>`, `intent=leave`)
+  before it starts; a refused channel is not started and the refusal is
+  printed. Quickstart labels every channel "off until OpenVault leave-machine
+  allows it".
+- The channel server banner says Crew Edge.
+- Gate module: `crates/zeroclaw-providers/src/netie.rs`. Session wrapper:
+  `crates/zeroclaw-infra/src/ids_only.rs`. Gate test:
+  `crates/zeroclaw-runtime/src/netie_gate.rs`
+  (`cargo test -p zeroclaw-runtime --lib netie_gate`).
+
+## Not done yet (stage 3)
+
+- Crate, package and binary names are still `zeroclaw*` (every workspace crate,
+  hundreds of paths); the `zeroclaw` CLI help text, `~/.zeroclaw` config dir,
+  `ZEROCLAW_*` env vars, systemd unit and web dashboard strings are upstream's.
+- An already-configured vendor provider with its own `api_key` still works; only
+  the subscription-login families are refused at the factory.
+- Codex (`requires_openai_auth`) and Claude setup-token credentials already on
+  disk are not refused at request time, only at Quickstart.
+- Whether OpenVault needs a seat token on `/v1` or serves `/v1/models`, and
+  whether it registers tool ids under kind `runtime` and channel ids under
+  `service`, is not measured. The gate sends no seat token.
+- Conversation text can still persist outside the session store: memory
+  backends, the ACP session store, cost and observability logs. Not gated.
+- Cron delivery to a channel (`build_channel_map`) and one-shot sends are not
+  behind the leave-machine ask; only channel startup is.
 - SECURITY, SUPPORT and CONTRIBUTING contacts and URLs still point at upstream.
 - Translated docs, changelogs and third-party notices are untouched.
-- Netie gate wiring: Same as crew-agent. NOTICE and both license files stay (Apache-2.0 requires NOTICE retention).
